# Sprint M2.01C — the derived vector-index runtime artifact (RO-09 items 3-5).
# The FAISS binary and its generated metadata are rebuildable runtime state, not
# repository source; the canonical corpus remains the source of truth. RO-09
# reserved this rule for M2.01C, once the runtime location existed. The path is
# sample_rag/vector_index/ (VECTOR_INDEX_ROOT) — the directory, not
# sample_rag/vector_index.py, which is source and is committed.
sample_rag/vector_index/

# Sprint M2.18 — the derived execution-evidence runtime artifact (RO-15
# Decision 8). Trace records are query-derived evidence about completed runs,
# not repository source: RO-15 classifies them in the same class RO-09 fixed
# for the FAISS index, and requires them to be excluded from Git tracking. The
# rule mirrors that precedent structurally — the path is scripts/execution_trace/
# (TRACE_ROOT), the directory, not scripts/execution_trace.py, which is source
# and is committed. Traces may also carry resume/job corpus content, which is a
# second and separate reason not to track them.
scripts/execution_trace/
